# Performance of the motions (21 October 2026)

Goal set by Matthieu on 21 October 2026: every motion plays at 60 Hz, even on a weak CPU, and the Validate page never freezes. FR : chaque motion tient 60 Hz, meme sur un CPU faible.

## The three benches (Scripts/)

| Command | What it measures |
|---|---|
| `node Scripts/PerfBench.mjs --trace [--budget 8 --known bmw-zhong-kui,cinematic-shot] [--out f.json] [id ...]` | every motion of the Validate list, three windows of 2 s each; ms per frame of the main thread, raster, compositor, software draw; exit code 1 over budget |
| `node Scripts/PerfValidate.mjs` | the Validate page: load, full scroll, long tasks (> 16 ms) |
| `node Scripts/PerfValidatePlay.mjs id ...` | one card played inside the real page: frames per second and thread time (`ZS_DPR=2` for a retina screen) |

`--css '<rule>'` (or `ZS_CSS`) injects a rule to find what costs: `*{filter:none!important}`, `.zs-dz{will-change:transform}`...
The bench runs in the managed chrome-headless-shell with SOFTWARE rendering: it is a pessimistic stand-in for a low CPU, not a GPU measure.

