Still above 8, declared: Zhong Kui (16, a whole 1600 x 668 plane moves every frame while the brush writes: the software draw floor) and cinematic-shot (13, two full 3D planes with SVG blurs).
In the real page each card plays at 60 frames per second (retina included), except cinematic-shot (49).

## Causes found, and the rule each one gives

1. SVG filter or mask region in `userSpaceOnUse` is computed over its whole area every frame: bound it to the box of what it treats (Zhong Kui: 4000 x 4000 blur and 6000 x 6000 mask per stroke).
2. A CSS mask on a line repaints its letters at each step: mask a WRAPPER the size of the ink, promote the line to its own layer (`will-change: transform`).
3. `blur(0px)` left after a tween keeps one render surface per letter: remove the filter when the tween ends.
4. Validate: builds are queued, one per screen refresh, visible first; the slider and the clock are written at 10 Hz while playing.
